    ('116', 'BUILD FIRST (before the crew use the jetway HMI) - Staff live their own lives: home, commute, 8-hour shifts (owner, 2026-11-18). Every member of your staff - gate agents and all the rest of the crew - is a real person in the world with their own life: (1) HOME: each lives in a house or flat in the same town as you (the town is coming later - its homes are the places this system uses; until it is built, a placeholder home address per person in the town area); (2) GETTING TO WORK: before their shift they leave home and come to the airport by their own car (drives the real roads, parks in the staff car park) or by bus (walks to a stop, rides the bus, walks in) - never appearing out of nowhere; (3) CLOCKING IN: they walk in through the staff entrance, change if their job has a uniform, and go to where their duty is; (4) THE SHIFT: an 8-hour shift per agent, from a rota (early / day / late / night, days off, holidays, sick days), following their duty list for that shift - a gate agent walks to the gate and the jetway console about 20 minutes before an arrival, does the T-10 jetway preparation on the HMI, docks it only when the aircraft is parked with engines and beacon off, undocks before departure; breaks on the shift; (5) GOING HOME: when the 8 hours are over they hand over to the next shift, clock out, change, walk out to their car or the bus stop and go home; (6) the rota makes sure every duty is covered at every hour (a missing person = a late flight); the same daily life later for every job (ground crew, fire crew, security, shops, cleaners ...). Needs: a person record (name, home, job, shift pattern, car or bus), the rota, the route planner home <-> airport (roads, bus line), the staff car park and staff entrance, and the duty system the jetway HMI, boarding and deboarding hang on.', '3-5 days (rough, to be split into parts)', ['none'], '', False),
