    ('82', 'Clouds: much faster, and a quality slider (owner, 2026-11-17: Clear shows broken clouds and the fps drops below 20; without clouds 50-60). Found by reading the code, to be confirmed with a GPU profile: 1) Clear is not clear - the cloud material treats coverage as plus/minus round its own default, so our 0.02 still gives broken cover, and the clouds are drawn even when none should show; 2) the sky light recaptures the whole sky with its clouds again every frame (real-time capture); 3) the engine sample cloud material is heavy (layers, storm and lightning layers, 3D noise) traced through a 10 km thick layer (5-15 km) at 3840x1080. Fix without losing the look: Clear = clouds off (none drawn), a lighter own cloud material, fewer samples where unseen (the cloud layer height and thickness NOT changed by hand - owner, 2026-11-17: the real-world weather data decides cloud height, type, rain, snow, wind, thunder, updrafts, for the whole world), the sky light recapture slowed (it changes slowly); then Settings > Graphics > Effects: Clouds on/off + quality slider. Stress test before/after', '4-6 h (rough, not measured)', ['gfx'], '', False),
